{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '17,31p'; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '196,207p'; git status --porcelain\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '17,31p'; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '196,207p'; git status --porcelain\"","aggregated_output":"    17\t- a clean material working copy.\n    18\t\n    19\tWith a usable base, the run executes the changed-scope selection between the two heads. That selection ignores the canonical result file and the derived administrative records that material bindings already ignore: the engine's closed list, still regular files at `HEAD`. It copies the base results of every unselected module. Each copied result keeps its outcome and states the head where it really ran (`carried_from`) and when (`carried_generated_at`). The delivery reading uses that head for the result. Any unmet condition runs everything and records the reason.\n    20\t\n    21\tA module may declare `\"selfContained\": true` in its metadata. A change outside every module then stops selecting it. The declaration is the instance's statement that the module's checks read only its own directory and its declared dependencies, so it applies to `--changed-from` too. Without it, the existing safe fallback stays.\n    22\t\n    23\t## Consequences\n    24\t\n    25\tA change confined to one module reruns that module, its declared dependents and the modules that cannot claim self-containment. Everything else is reused with its true origin visible. Consumers that compare a result's head with a subject head now see carried results as observations of the earlier head, which is accurate. An incorrect `selfContained` declaration can carry a stale result. That risk sits with the instance's explicit declaration and is documented next to it.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Alternatives considered\n    28\t\n    29\t- Hashing each check's declared inputs would be more precise. It needs every check's inputs declared and verified, and it is a larger contract.\n    30\t- Merging a partial `--changed-from` record into the canonical file by hand would hide which results were reused.\n    31\t- Carrying across matrix or engine changes would make a definition change invisible to the evidence.\n   196\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun test:TestCarryRefusesAFilteredBase test:TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy test:TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds test:TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial test:TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory test:TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead test:TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink test:TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule test:TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath test:TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths test:TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem test:TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs test:TestValidateUntrackedMaterialCreatedDuringTheRunIsNotClean test:TestCarryRefusesAnAliasingSymlinkInsideASubmodule test:TestCarryDetectsACaseFoldedDirectory test:TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule test:TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor\n   197\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule test:TestCarryRecordFileIsNotAChange test:TestCarryIgnoresDerivedAdministrativeRecords test:TestCarrySelectsAModuleWithoutAPriorResult\n   198\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestCarryKeepsTheOriginalHeadAcrossChainedCarries test:TestCarryKeepsACarriedFailureAFailure\n   199\t- R5 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule\n   200\t- R6 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRootChangeRunsEverythingUnlessSelfContained test:TestChangedScopeHonoursSelfContainedModules test:TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename test:TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName test:TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles test:TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents test:TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata test:TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents test:TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents test:TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles test:TestChangedScopeEvaluatesEveryDeclaredDependency test:TestChangedScopeDiscoveredAncestorDependencySelectsItsDependents test:TestChangedScopeIgnoresSubmoduleHidingConfiguration test:TestChangedScopeSelectsTheEnclosingModule test:TestChangedScopeRootModuleEnclosesEveryModule\n   201\t- R7 [satisfied] test:TestDeliveryValidationRunReadsTheCarriedHead\n   202\t- R8 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRecordFileIsNotAChange\n   203\t- R9 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun\n   204\t- R10 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun\n   205\t\n   206\tR9 is enforced by `safeGitRevRE` in `planCarry` before any Git call; the not-an-ancestor case drives a forged head through it. R10 is the `base without engine version` case.\n   207\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
