{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --porcelain; git diff --quiet; git diff --cached --quiet; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '185,193p'\"","aggregated_output":"   185\t- 2026-11-23: review round 9 (rrn-dfc7e3348240ce19) found N24–N26.\n   186\t  - N24: gitlinks inside a module were not scanned.\n   187\t  - N25: an enclosing module was not selected when a nested module changed.\n   188\t  - N26: case folding in ancestor directories of a dependency.\n   189\t  All three are fixed, and the lead extended N25 so the root module encloses every module. Each regression test failed when its fix was mutated out.\n   190\t\n   191\t### Results summary\n   192\tAll new and existing tests pass, and the strict matrix is green. In this repository, `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so carrying saves little here. In an instance with many modules, a change confined to one of them reruns only that module and the modules that are not declared self-contained.\n   193\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nTwo high-severity blockers remain: case-fold detection can fail open, and declared dependencies can escape the repository. A low-severity ADR wording defect also remains.\n\nTargeted tests, race tests, build, vet, and artifact-check passed. Both strict validators failed one required check; their truncated output prevents reliable identification. Direct `go test ./...` timed out. The sealed passing evidence remains distinct from these reruns.\n\nApplied Go backend, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were written. The failed required validators prevent a completed validation attestation.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N27\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 479,\n      \"summary\": \"casefoldedDirectory returns false when Stat of its first caseable entry fails. An allowed dangling symlink can therefore hide a case-folded ancestor. Use case-folded shared with case-sensitive child shared/a, modules shared/a and b, and b declaring dependsOn=[\\\"shared/A/input\\\"]. Add shared/0-dangling -> ../unowned-missing, which the tracked-symlink guard permits because neither endpoint intersects a module or dependency. The ancestor probe stops at this dangling entry without testing a/A. After a passing baseline, changing shared/a/input selects shared/a but misses b's differently cased dependency, allowing a stale pass to be carried. Ancestor enumeration alone does not establish R2 or D1. Treat unreadable probes conservatively and continue past unusable entries; add a dangling-entry regression. Established by source trace and an in-memory predicate model; the mixed-filesystem scenario was not exercised on matching hardware.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N28\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 55,\n      \"summary\": \"loadScopeMetadata accepts dependsOn paths outside the repository without confinement. A self-contained b declaring dependsOn=[\\\"../shared/input\\\"] can legitimately read that declared input, pass a full baseline, and then receive a carried pass after the external input changes. Superproject status and diff cannot observe the change; declaredDependencyHits cannot match the outside path, and carryRelevantDirs stops when the dependency escapes root. No eligibility guard refuses it. This breaks D1's unchanged-input guarantee without an incorrect selfContained declaration. Reject absolute and root-escaping dependency paths before allowing carry, with an actionable fallback reason, and cover the external-input sequence. Established by source inspection and an in-memory path/selection probe, not a newly executed fixture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N29\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"summary\": \"The consequences paragraph says a module-local change reruns every module that cannot claim self-containment. Runtime behavior and TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule show that an unrelated ordinary module is carried. The non-self-contained fallback applies when a changed file has no module owner. Correct this paragraph and the matching statement in the spec's results summary at line 192.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N24\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:407-424 scans every gitlink without the former ownership filter. TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule passed in the targeted carry test run and the race-enabled run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N25\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:165-168 selects enclosing modules, including root. TestChangedScopeSelectsTheEnclosingModule and TestChangedScopeRootModuleEnclosesEveryModule passed in the targeted and race-enabled runs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N26\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:434-461 now enumerates ancestors, and TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor passed. The resulting protection remains incomplete because casefoldedDirectory can return false before probing the folding ancestor's usable entries; see N27 at validate_carry.go:477-479.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the complete implementation diff, spec R1-R10, decisions D1-D3, ADR, CLI/help, English and Portuguese manuals and scaffold, result publication, delivery parsing and downstream freshness/compaction. Swept gitlinks, nested and unavailable submodules, symlinks, case aliases and ancestor probes, dependency confinement, manifest-free moduleOverrides, nested ownership, stack/check changes with an unchanged matrix, criticality and transitive widening, chained provenance, cancellation, and concurrent canonical publication. Targeted carry/changed-scope/engine/reader tests and race-enabled CLI tests passed; build and vet passed. Artifact-check passed with provenance warnings. Both strict validators completed with one required-check failure: repository-wide 235/236 passed and component 232/233 passed. The captured output was truncated, so the failing check was not identified. Direct go test ./... timed out in internal/pose after ten minutes. Persisting assessments were not run because scratch creation was denied. New functional findings are source-established with in-memory models, not filesystem reproductions. Final Git status and tracked/index diffs were clean.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-bd2666392e9e4697\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined D1-D3 and eligibility/selection assumptions. Verified prior regressions through targeted tests. Distinguished trusted instance declarations and permitted unstamped engine identities from the unresolved mixed-filesystem hardware scenario. N27 and N28 identify unsupported input-equivalence assumptions; neither is accepted as a risk.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Carried entries remain silent and bypass execution workers; canonical publication retains the governance guard and atomic publisher. Targeted race-enabled tests passed. Reviewed cancellation and last-writer publication behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Result fields are additive, schema-1 reading remains compatible, and delivery parsing substitutes carried head/time while retaining existing provenance fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N28\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Decoded dependency metadata is accepted without repository confinement; unsupported inputs silently narrow execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integrity-index-compaction-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced carried head/time from the canonical reader through delivery results and compaction. The targeted reader regression passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed fallback reasons, selection explanations, carried counts, outcomes, and preservation of bounded/redacted output. Targeted tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined CLI flag refusals, additive file fields, legacy records, and MCP boundaries. Existing records retain their reading semantics; bases without engine identity are refused for reuse.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N27\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A case-folded ancestor can evade the eligibility guard and permit a currently failing consumer check to retain a carried pass. N28 provides a separate unchanged-input counterexample.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N27\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 correctly ties reuse to unchanged module inputs, but the implemented alias guard does not establish that premise in all accepted configurations. N28 also leaves declared external inputs unattributable.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records the decision to preserve original check observations while binding the new run at HEAD, conditional on unchanged inputs; it also explains declarations and conservative fallback.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N29\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Manual/help/scaffold behavior was compared with runtime. The ADR and spec results summary overstate which ordinary modules rerun for module-local changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N28\",\n      \"rationale\": \"An external declared dependency receives neither an actionable refusal nor a full-run fallback, although the engine cannot establish its unchanged state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N27\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed R1-R10 and their regression traces. R2's case-sensitive-directory condition and D1's input-equivalence premise remain unproven in N27; N28 exposes another accepted configuration outside Git's observation boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-bd2666392e9e4697\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Changes remain within the declared carry planning, shared selection, structured-result reader, CLI/help, governance, and documentation scope. No unrelated feature or dependency expansion was found.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N28\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Git revision arguments are confined and modified engines refuse reuse, but dependency paths can escape the repository's evidence boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-bd2666392e9e4697\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module selection with whole-matrix/engine equality is proportionate compared with arbitrary per-check input hashing. Conservative refusal is the smallest sufficient treatment of unattributable inputs. The choice would need reconsideration if cross-engine reuse or external-input tracking became requirements; N27 and N28 require completing the current conservative boundary.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully with exit 0. Output included provenance warnings and the trailer-resolved range, which extends through index commits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-bd2666392e9e4697\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose assess design --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --json. Its digest matches the sealed structural evidence and identifies the ADR delta.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This assessment persists files. Scratch creation failed with Read-only file system, so it was not run against the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required scratch copy could not be created. Inspected producer/consumer code and sealed integration evidence instead of persisting assessment output in the checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Scratch creation was denied. Reviewed changed implementation paths directly; no assessment output was written.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only precondition: POSE must first record and verify the review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until POSE records the conclusion; the user explicitly prohibits recording an attestation during this review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved and applied backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules, with delivery-evidence review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose validate --strict: exit 1, 235 of 236 checks passed, one required check failed. Captured output was truncated, preventing reliable identification of that check. The cited sealed unit evidence passed previously and is not presented as evidence that this rerun passed. A successful current full-gate result remains outstanding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp: exit 1, 232 of 233 checks passed, one required check failed. The failure identity was lost in truncated capture. Targeted unit/race tests, build and vet passed; direct unsharded go test ./... timed out at ten minutes in internal/pose. The sealed passing unit reference remains distinct from this failed validator.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
